# OPDP import

Import HostTools from "./host_tools.lg".
Import OpdpImportRules from "./opdp_import_rules.lg".
Import WireRead from "./wire_read.lg".

`factory coordinator import-opdp <pin.json> <atlas.json.gz> <work-dir>` imports
every problem of the Ulam OPDP difficulty atlas into the coordinator so workers
can lease it: the release is refused unless its SHA-256 is the one the pin
(`ops/factory/opdp.pin.json`) names; it is decompressed and cut into pieces in
`work-dir` by `gzip`, `sed` and `split`; each record becomes a problem, its node
under its cohort, source collection and category, and its profile; then every
open problem without a unit gets one (`opdp_plan.lg`), and the counts are checked
against the pin. Every statement is an upsert, so running it again changes
nothing but ranks.

## Note
The release cut into line pieces: a new line before every record start, then
pieces of at most eight megabytes that end at line ends.

## To prepareSteps () -> Text:
    Let mutable q be ["set -eu; rm -rf \"$2/parts\"; mkdir -p \"$2/parts\";"].
    Push "gzip -dc \"$1\" | sed 's/{{\"problem_id\":/\\n&/g' > \"$2/atlas.lines\";" to q.
    Push "split -C 8M -d -a 5 \"$2/atlas.lines\" \"$2/parts/atlas.\"; rm -f \"$2/atlas.lines\"" to q.
    Return join(q, " ").

## Note
A tool's output, or why it failed.

## To toolOutput (program: Text, arguments: Seq of Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect runTool(program, arguments, 1800000, 1048576):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error program + ": " + e.
        When Ok (r):
            If r's exitCode is not equal to 0:
                Return a new Err with error program + " failed: " + r's stderr.
            Return a new Ok with value r's stdout.
    Return a new Err with error program + ": unrun".

## Note
The pin's cohort labels by cohort key, after the release's hash is checked.

## To checkedPin (pinPath: Text, atlasPath: Text) -> Result of Json and Text:
    Inspect read(pinPath):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "cannot read the pin: " + e.
        When Ok (pinText):
            Let pin be jsonParse(pinText).
            Inspect toolOutput("sha256sum", [atlasPath]):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error e.
                When Ok (out):
                    Let actual be item 1 of split(trim(out), " ").
                    If actual is not equal to textAt(pin, "sha256") or length of actual is not equal to 64:
                        Return a new Err with error "the release's sha256 is " + actual + ", the pin names " + textAt(pin, "sha256").
                    Return a new Ok with value pin.
    Return a new Err with error "no pin".

## To cohortLabels (pin: Json) -> Map of Text to Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Map of Text to Text.
    Inspect jsonGet(pin, "cohorts"):
        When JObj (entries):
            Repeat for en in entries:
                Set out at cohortKeyOf(en's key) to textAt(en's val, "label").
        Otherwise:
            Return out.
    Return out.
